Subject: Settle the SSA in one pass, fix the promotion cap, retry conservatively

What this does
  Settle the SSA in one pass, fix the promotion cap, retry conservatively.

Why we need it
  Three refusals a valid program could reach: the SSA's merge ran after the whole simulate sweep, so a chain of more than 4096 blocks settled one block per pass and was refused; the promotion cap set `ns_ok = 0` without clearing `slot_ok`/`ok_index`, so the home scan recorded ids whose arrays were never allocated and the simulator read a NULL `sval` (SIGSEGV); and a function with more than 4096 registers had no fallback.

What it adds
  Merge and simulate in one ascending sweep (back edges still carry values across passes) with `out[]` initialized to -1; clear the eligibility bits with the count exactly as `REGVM_NOPROMO` does; and retry the whole build once with `fd->regvm_conservative` (no promotion, reuse, folding, hoisting or light frame) before leaving a function refused. A final refusal asserts under `QJS_REGVM_VERIFY` with the site's reason; the refusal report moved to the final path so a retried success is not reported.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
